spec: S01-10

Setup happens once; a second `serve --setup-only` on the same store says so and exits 0.

```console
$ ANNOTARY_HOME=cdhome ANNOTARY_SETUP_HANDLE=rowan ANNOTARY_SETUP_NAME=Rowan annotary serve --setup-only
Tenant created at [..]/cdhome/store
  owner handle [rowan]: rowan
  display name [[..]]: Rowan
  local password (blank = loopback trust, browser is you): 
Vault "notes" created.
Owner token for the CLI (shown once) — put it in your shell or a profile in [..]/cdhome/config.toml:

  ANNOTARY_TOKEN=ant_[..]

No CLI credential is saved: export the token above, or run `annotary login` (needs the local password); `annotary member add <handle>` adds a Member and mints their token.

$ ANNOTARY_HOME=cdhome annotary serve --setup-only
store [..]/cdhome/store is already set up (owner @rowan)

```
